# Performance Rules

- `ListView.builder` for large lists — never `Column`/`Row` with many children
- `const` constructors for static widgets to reduce rebuild overhead
- Avoid expensive operations in `build()` — use builders or separate widgets
- `RepaintBoundary` for complex custom painters
- Use isolates (`compute()`) for CPU-intensive operations
- Lazy loading and pagination for large datasets
- Profile with Flutter DevTools regularly

## Big-O (data-flow, separate from cyclomatic)

- Optimize only when behavior **understood and preserved**; small proven fix > rewrite.
- On "analyze/audit/scan/report" — report only, no file edits unless implement asked.
- Full catalog (transformations · safety · what-not-to-do): skill `flutter-performance`.
- Scanner: `python3 ~/.cursor/skills/flutter-performance/scripts/analyze_complexity.py . --format markdown` (Dart-aware).
- Record vs class (hot loop, constant-factor; tiebreaker, not a default type choice — outside hot loops semantics decide): hashing / `Map`/`Set` key → record; frequent `==` → data class; plain data → no difference.
